CUE's struct shorthand, a: b: c, in a schema and in a lens body. A version
file writes every struct with its braces; the shorthand is refused wherever
it appears, and Format expands it.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
schema: {
	meta: owner: string
}
-- ship/1.0.thema --
schema: {
	meta: {
		owner: string
		team:  string
	}
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: meta: team: "unassigned"
}
-- out/error --
v1_0: meta: ... is CUE's struct shorthand, which a version file does not use: write v1_0: {meta: ...}:
    1.0.thema:10:8
meta: team: ... is CUE's struct shorthand, which a version file does not use: write meta: {team: ...}:
    1.0.thema:10:14
meta: owner: ... is CUE's struct shorthand, which a version file does not use: write meta: {owner: ...}:
    history/0.0.thema:2:8
